-## Completion and dispatch prerequisites
-
-The persisted operational issue result and reconciled criteria are sufficient
-result delivery. Optional comments cannot block an otherwise authorized child
-completion. Read back the result and terminal state; preserve a single native
-parent wake and reconcile ambiguous responses before any retry. Integration
-adapters must support assignment-launched work with no comment thread.
-
-Before dispatching a stage, resolve its repository baseline from the owning
-declaration and compare required capabilities with the chosen execution target.
-A later stage's missing capabilities need not block independent implementation.
-Separate requested deliverables, required validation and optional operational
-rehearsal at intake. Real releases, installation, credentials or a specific
-production version are not implicit requirements of tooling development.
-
-Recovery follows the actual failure: fix defects and refresh affected evidence;
-resume interrupted evaluation after prerequisites are repaired; reconcile failed
-communication without repeating engineering work. Preserve fresh independent
-acceptance for a new verdict. Escalation records identify recipient, question,
-evidence, next action and delivery acknowledgement; absent delivery is an
-integration limitation, not a user decision.
